00:38:06.729 --> 00:38:08.209
So what is a tiff district?

00:38:09.110 --> 00:38:12.830
The creation of a tax increment financing or TIFF district is a tool that

00:38:12.830 --> 00:38:15.949
allows municipalities to complete public infrastructure improvements.

00:38:16.780 --> 00:38:20.459
Uh, by using increment tax revenue or future revenue streams,

00:38:20.699 --> 00:38:23.850
not any existing revenue streams within that district,

00:38:24.179 --> 00:38:28.300
those existing revenue streams continue to flow through the tax recipients

00:38:28.300 --> 00:38:29.159
as they do today.

00:38:30.149 --> 00:38:31.610
Uh, the principle is very simple.

00:38:31.840 --> 00:38:36.340
The city makes public, uh, improvements in a defined geographic area,

00:38:36.520 --> 00:38:37.840
the district, if you will.

00:38:38.590 --> 00:38:42.830
With the intent of stimulating new private investment or new economic development

00:38:42.830 --> 00:38:45.580
within that district or that boundary, uh,

00:38:45.639 --> 00:38:50.469
as new development occurs, the taxable value or that new tax base that's

00:38:50.469 --> 00:38:55.030
being created by those new investments go with stay within the district

00:38:55.030 --> 00:38:59.370
to pay off projects if they're paid for by cash or the or debt service.

00:39:00.120 --> 00:39:04.530
And then as you roll through that and you pay off those bonds or you pay

00:39:04.530 --> 00:39:10.770
off that project, uh, the TI district is closed and all new tax recipients

00:39:10.770 --> 00:39:14.770
or the tax recipients receive their proportion of those new taxes that were

00:39:14.770 --> 00:39:17.610
created as a result of those public investments.

00:39:19.709 --> 00:39:23.879
Uh, one misunderstanding that sometimes people think is,

00:39:24.479 --> 00:39:25.969
are we increasing taxes?

00:39:26.439 --> 00:39:26.760
No.

00:39:27.530 --> 00:39:32.330
Uh, by the Alabama Constitution, it takes a vote of the people to increase

00:39:32.330 --> 00:39:36.330
any property tax, i.e., the millage rate for Madison County.

00:39:36.409 --> 00:39:38.689
For all of us combined, it's 58 mils.

00:39:39.040 --> 00:39:43.830
Uh, the creation of Tith District keeps that millage at 58 mils.

00:39:44.250 --> 00:39:44.810
Uh, the.

00:39:45.169 --> 00:39:49.080
The city of Huntsville administration or the city council adjust anybody's

00:39:49.080 --> 00:39:49.729
property taxes.

00:39:49.830 --> 00:39:53.939
We actually have elected officials, the county tax assessor that evaluates

00:39:53.939 --> 00:39:57.879
all taxes within the county and provides that assessment.

00:39:58.209 --> 00:40:02.100
So the city council nor the Madison County commission passing a TI district

00:40:02.100 --> 00:40:06.300
does nothing to affect one's individuality of their tax base.

00:40:06.459 --> 00:40:08.330
That's done by the tax assessor.

00:40:10.959 --> 00:40:15.360
Lastly, no, as I've mentioned, no existing tax revenues dedicated for schools.

00:40:15.429 --> 00:40:18.719
The county or city budgets were reduced, um,

00:40:18.919 --> 00:40:20.860
or diverted within a tip district.

00:40:21.000 --> 00:40:24.879
It's only the new tax base or the increment growth within that district

00:40:24.879 --> 00:40:25.899
that is captured.

